= Topological facts about orthogonal groups


- $"SO"(n)$ is connected @lawson1989
- $"SO"(p, q)$ for $p, q >= 1$ has exactly two connected components lawson1989
- $"Spin"(V, g)$ is a #link("https://mathworld.wolfram.com/UniversalCover.html")[universal cover] of $"SO"(V, g)$
